Description: let the session choose the primary monitor
 Over Wayland, libxfce4windowing learns the primary output only from Xfce's own
 compositor, through a private protocol. Under any other compositor (labwc, for
 Dodobian) it guesses: a laptop panel, else the monitor at 0,0, else the first.
 With a monitor on the left that is not the main one, the guess is wrong, and
 xfdesktop puts the desktop icons there.
 .
 Moving the main monitor to 0,0 and the left one to negative coordinates does
 move the icons, but it breaks X11 programs: the XWayland root then starts at
 the main monitor, and windows on the left one stop receiving the pointer.
 .
 This patch reads XFW_PRIMARY_MONITOR before guessing: a connector name, or
 several separated by commas, the first connected one winning.
Author: The Dodobian authors
Forwarded: not-yet
Last-Update: 2026-11-24
